--- !u!114 &6497004537407849551
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1987288787362968937}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 62b3bcbdce6b7fa409c336af049ab53b, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Timer: 4
  stringList:
  - "<color=red>This is an emergency message:</color>\r\n\r\n<color=cyan>- Terrorist
    known as \"Creepy Cat\" arrested by \r\npolice after 1 year on the run! He said
    during\r\nhis arrest!\r\n\r\n\"Let me sleep in peace! or I'll poop in your garden...\"\r\n\r\nHe
    is currently in a secret prison....</color>\r\n\r\n<color=orange>This is a network
    message:</color>\r\n\r\n<color=cyan>- Error 8: Unable to Establish the VPN \r\nConnection
    (error 800)</color>\r\n\r\n<color=orange>LUNA INDUSTRIES LTD MESSAGE:</color>\r\n\r\n<color=cyan>-
    Integrate AI Accelerator ECS for your \r\nreal-time use cases and show real-time
    predictions\r\nand NBA recommendations on one component.</color>\n"
  - "<color=orange>What is ECS?:</color>\r\n\r\n<color=cyan>- The Elastic Common
    Schema (ECS)\r\nis an open source specification, developed \r\nwith support from
    the Elastic user community. \r\n\r\nECS defines a common set of fields to be
    used \r\nwhen storing event data in Elasticsearch, such \r\nas logs and metrics.</color>\r\n\r\n<color=orange>My
    events don\u2019t map with ECS:</color>\r\n\r\n<color=cyan>- ECS is a permissive
    schema. If your \r\nevents have additional data that cannot be mapped\r\nto ECS,
    you can simply add them to your events,\r\nusing custom field names.</color>\n"
  - "<color=orange>Project Maturity:</color>\r\n\r\n<color=cyan>- ECS improvements
    are released following\r\nSemantic Versioning. Major ECS releases are planned
    \r\nto be aligned with major releases.\r\n\r\nAny feedback on the general structure,
    missing fields\r\nor existing fields is appreciated. For contributions\r\nplease
    read the LUNA LTD Contribution Guidelines.</color>\r\n\r\n<color=orange>Schema:</color>\r\n\r\n<color=cyan>-
    ECS is a permissive schema. If your \r\nevents have additional data that cannot
    be mapped\r\nto ECS, you can simply add them to your events, using\r\ncustom
    field names.</color>\n"
  textObject: {fileID: 5278186201817001873}
